# CIFAR-10 Image Classifier

TensorFlow/Keras project for training and evaluating an image classifier on CIFAR-10. Training reads images and labels from the local `cifar-10-batches-py` folder

## Requirements

- Python 3.10 or newer (3.11+ recommended)

## Dataset

Place the official CIFAR-10 Python batches in the project root:

```
TensorFlow-Cursor/
  cifar-10-batches-py/
    data_batch_1
    data_batch_2
    ...
    test_batch
    batches.meta
```

Download from [https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html) and extract so the folder name is `cifar-10-batches-py`.

Training and test data can use different paths in `image_classifier/config.py`:

- `CIFAR10_BATCHES_DIR` — folder with `data_batch_1` … `data_batch_5` (training)
- `CIFAR10_TEST_BATCH_PATH` — path to the test pickle file (default: `CIFAR10_BATCHES_DIR / "test_batch"`)

## Install dependencies

From the project root (`TensorFlow-Cursor`):

### Windows (PowerShell)

```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### macOS / Linux

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Libraries installed

| Package      | Purpose                                      |
|-------------|-----------------------------------------------|
| tensorflow  | Model training, evaluation, inference         |
| numpy       | Array handling and metrics                    |
| Pillow      | Image I/O (used by TensorFlow image utilities) |
| openpyxl    | Normalized confusion matrix Excel export      |

## Run the code

Activate the virtual environment, then run commands from the project root.

### 1. Train (Not required as file already contains a trained model)

Default: transfer learning (MobileNetV2 + classification head).

```powershell
python -m image_classifier.train
```

Outputs:

- `checkpoints/best_model.keras` — best validation checkpoint
- `checkpoints/class_names.json` — class names in label order
- `saved_model/model.keras` — final model after training
- `saved_model/class_names.json`

### 2. Evaluate on the test set

Uses the test batch at `CIFAR10_TEST_BATCH_PATH` (by default `cifar-10-batches-py/test_batch`) and prints accuracy, Cohen's kappa, weighted F1, and a classification report. Writes a normalized confusion matrix to Excel by default.

```powershell
# Test best model
python -m image_classifier.evaluate --model checkpoints/best_model.keras

Options:

```powershell
# test most recent model
python -m image_classifier.evaluate
```

# Skip Excel export
python -m image_classifier.evaluate --excel-out ""

# Less console output
python -m image_classifier.evaluate --quiet

# Different test batch file (overrides config.CIFAR10_TEST_BATCH_PATH)
python -m image_classifier.evaluate --test-batch path/to/test_batch
```

### 3. Predict on image files

```powershell
python -m image_classifier.predict path/to/image1.jpg path/to/image2.png
```


## Configuration

Switch dataset mode in `image_classifier/dataset_source.py`:

- `cifar10` — local `cifar-10-batches-py` (default)
- `image_directory` — class folders under `data/train/` (see `DATA_DIR` in config)

## Project layout

```
image_classifier/
  config.py          # Hyperparameters and paths
  dataset.py         # CIFAR-10 batch loading and tf.data pipelines
  dataset_source.py  # Active dataset selector
  model.py           # CNN and transfer-learning architectures
  train.py           # Training entry point
  evaluate.py        # Test-set evaluation and metrics
  predict.py         # Inference on arbitrary images
checkpoints/         # Created when training
saved_model/         # Created when training
```

## Troubleshooting

- **ModuleNotFoundError: image_classifier** — Run commands from the project root, not from inside `image_classifier/`.
- **Cannot activate venv on Windows** — If scripts are blocked: `Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned`, then activate again.
- **Missing CIFAR batches** — Ensure `cifar-10-batches-py` exists next to `image_classifier/` and contains `data_batch_1` … `data_batch_5` and `test_batch`.
